mode: "100644"
text: "# The VOUCH framework — real proof that actually converts\n\nA testimonial is someone vouching for you. The job is to make that vouch **real, specific, objection-matched,\nand credible** — never to manufacture it. Each letter is a gate; most weak proof content fails at U (no\nspecifics) or skips V (consent/authenticity).\n\n## V — Vet real proof\nSource genuine proof — reviews, testimonials, DMs, UGC, case studies, results — and verify it's real before it\nbecomes content:\n- **Consent first.** Get explicit permission to feature the person + their words/face; a public tag is *not*\n  blanket permission, and **paid/ads use needs separate, broader rights.**\n- **Never fabricate.** No invented testimonials, no AI-generated \"customers\", no putting words in a real\n  customer's mouth. (FTC rule + the 2026 likeness crisis: no real-or-AI lookalike without permission.)\n- **Disclose** material connections (employee/paid/gifted); never condition an incentive on positive sentiment.\n- **Preserve meaning** when you trim a quote.\n\n## O — Overcome the right objection\nProof only works when it answers the **specific doubt** in the buyer's head. Map proof to objection:\nprice → ROI/value proof; risk → guarantee + \"people like me\" proof; \"will it work for *me*?\" → a near-identical\ncustomer's result; trust → volume + recognizable names. Right proof, right funnel stage — objection-dissolving\nproof sits near the decision point.\n\n## U — Unearth the specifics\nSpecificity is believability. Pull the concrete: a real **number** (time saved, revenue, % change), a\n**before/after**, a sensory detail, a real **face + first name + role** (with consent). Cut vague raves. And keep\nthe occasional **mixed/negative** note where honest — it raises credibility (a flawless wall reads fake).\n\n## C — Cast the customer as the hero\nFrame the proof as **their** story: where they were stuck → the turning point → the result they got. The customer\nis the hero; you're the guide (this is where it hands to `storytelling-and-narrative`). It should read as the\ncustomer winning, not the brand bragging.\n\n## H — Hand it across formats + placements\nOne proof asset → many cuts, routed to the writers and placed where doubt is highest:\n- **Quote/stat card** → caption-writer + design-and-templates. **Results carousel / case study** → carousel-writer.\n- **Video testimonial** → reels-script. **UGC reshare** (with rights + credit) → ugc-and-influencer pipeline.\n- **Placement:** decision points — product/landing context, launch posts, DMs (`social-selling-and-dm`), email\n  (`email-and-newsletter`), funnels (`lead-magnets-and-funnels`).\n- **WoopSocial publishes**; measure saves/shares + clicks; never fabricate a metric or a review.\n"
